# Cursor Rules for Supabase Integration

## Database Access
- You have access to the Supabase database schema defined in `src/types/database.ts`
- Use the API functions in `src/lib/api.ts` for database operations
- All database operations should be type-safe using the Database type

## Supabase Project Configuration
- Project URL: Use REACT_APP_SUPABASE_URL from environment
- API Key: Use REACT_APP_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY from environment
- Database Schema: Follow the structure in `src/types/database.ts`

## Direct Database Operations
You can help with:
- Writing SQL queries for Supabase
- Creating database migrations
- Setting up Row Level Security policies
- Managing database indexes
- Creating stored procedures and functions

## API Development
- Create new API endpoints using the existing patterns in `src/lib/api.ts`
- Implement real-time subscriptions
- Handle authentication and authorization
- Manage file uploads to Supabase Storage

## Database Schema Management
- Update the TypeScript types when schema changes
- Ensure type safety across all database operations
- Maintain consistency between database and application types

## Security Best Practices
- Always use Row Level Security (RLS) policies
- Validate input data before database operations
- Use parameterized queries to prevent SQL injection
- Implement proper error handling for database operations 